// Whether the page on screen still matches the document.
//
// Presenting the pixels again is cheap and laying the document out again is
// not, so a frame that changed nothing presents what it already has. A
// keystroke is the only thing that can change the document, and every one of
// them ends in ed_seek or ed_set, which is why this flag is raised in exactly
// two places.

ed_dirty() {
  int ret_i = (import ed_dty)[0];
} return int ret_i;
given ed_cur_init ():(1)
given ed_out_fixture given ed_cur_init given ed_flush ():(0)

ed_dirt(int v) {
  lset((import ed_dty), 0, v);
} return void;
given ed_cur_init (0):() then ed_dirty:(0)
given ed_cur_init (1):() then ed_dirty:(1)

// The frame handed to the window, and the page marked as matching it.
ed_flush() {
  ed_dirt(0);
